WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
(Transcribed by UniScribe (https://www.uniscribe.co). Upgrade to remove this message.)

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:01.789
Hi there! Welcome to Sprints.

00:00:01.849 --> 00:00:04.829
I'm Sarah Jenkins, Product Director of Learner Success.

00:00:04.829 --> 00:00:08.449
I'm really thrilled you're stepping up to lead our Talent Pipeline Optimization

00:00:08.449 --> 00:00:12.610
Project. Next quarter, our Employer Partnerships team is rolling out a massive

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:15.350
launch with a coalition of high-tier hiring partners.

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:19.430
Those partners are demanding complete transparency before committing to hiring.

00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:23.690
They need concrete evidence of learner performance, trajectories, and skill mastery.

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:28.530
But right now, our internal learner data is noisy, scattered across cohorts and

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:32.830
disconnected from Success for me looks like a unified,

00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:37.050
trustworthy system that translates learner achievements directly into employer

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:40.689
readiness, so partners can hire our graduates with complete confidence.

00:00:40.909 --> 00:00:43.410
In tackling this, we have two firm constraints.

00:00:43.629 --> 00:00:46.690
First, we have a hard two-week turnaround to deliver everything.

00:00:46.790 --> 00:00:51.450
And second, you have to build this end-to-end pipeline strictly using our existing

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:55.409
cohort records, without bringing in outside data or new commercial platforms.

00:00:55.489 --> 00:00:57.809
My biggest worry is partner trust.

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:04.249
or detached from real industry competencies, employers simply won't buy in.

00:01:04.249 --> 00:01:08.650
At our final presentation in two weeks, I expect to see a comprehensive analytical

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:12.430
pipeline, clean data transformations, engineered mastery indices,

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:16.249
and an actionable decision-making framework that clearly proves candidate value to

00:01:16.249 --> 00:01:19.969
hiring managers. You have the exact skillset we need to crack this open,

00:01:19.969 --> 00:01:21.790
and I cannot wait to see your work.

